═══ CONCLUSION — the lever generalizes across convention KINDS ═══
  Two unrelated conventions (string FORMAT v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>; name ORDERING LAST, FIRST), same AGENTS.md placement,
  same result: CC 0/12, ZAK 12/12, both at N=12 (Fisher exact p<1e-6 each). With the 12c control (CC 12/12 when the
  identical rule sits in CLAUDE.md, 0 reads → auto-fold), the claim is: on repos that carry their conventions in
  AGENTS.md, zakcode adheres and Claude Code 2.1.267 (headless) does not — because of what each loop FOLDS, not what
  the convention is about, and not discovery (thrust 8).

═══ NEXT: thrust 11 — the FOLD-CAP CLIFF (a first-principles check of the lever's own boundary) ═══
  The fold is capped and SILENT: prompt.py MAX_CONTEXT_FILE_CHARS = 8_192 per file, applied as
  content = raw.strip()[:8192] with NO omission note (prompt.py:499-500; identical in the zc-01 build; no test pins
  it). The sibling rules-file path DOES emit an omission note (ADR at docs/DECISIONS.md:4213-4217), and the ADR that
  set the guide caps rejected raising them ("the 35B's window is the constraint the budgets protect"). So a rule that
  starts past char 8,192 of a long, realistic AGENTS.md is CUT from the fold with nothing telling the model the
  guide is incomplete. Tasks (committed in this PR) hold 13's rule + verify byte-constant and vary only guide length:
    14o-agents-md-longguide-over  — 24-section realistic guide, 9,740 chars, rule header at char 8,760 → CUT
    14u-agents-md-longguide-under — same style, 7,637 chars, rule header at char 6,657 → KEPT (attention control)
  Both builders assert the cliff with the SAME .strip()[:8192] the fold applies (deterministic pre-check; a remote
  dry-build on zc-01 reproduced the local numbers exactly). PRE-REGISTERED: ZAK-14u ~12/12 (fold intact; measures
  dilution alone) | ZAK-14o DROPS toward CC's ~0/12 unless the survey listing prompts an agentic read — and a silent
  cut may be WORSE than CC, since the model believes it has the whole guide | CC-14o ≈ CC-14u ≈ 0/12 (no AGENTS.md
  fold either way). zakcode arms run first. If the cliff bites, fix candidates: (a) an omission note that NAMES the
  file and the cut ("AGENTS.md truncated at 8192 of N chars — read the file for the rest"), consistent with the
  rules-file precedent and with the campaign's own finding that a LISTING reliably prompts a read (06v); (b)
  MANDATORY-section-preserving truncation. Raising the cap is the ADR's rejected alternative. Batch staged on zc-01
  (t11_14longguide_batch.sh); results follow.

